# Local build artifacts, NOT uploaded to Vercel.
#
# Every directory pattern here is ANCHORED with a leading slash, which is the
# whole point: a bare `build/` is a gitignore-style pattern that matches a
# directory of that name at ANY depth, so it silently removed the Build Studio
# itself from the deployment --
#     src/app/build/page.tsx
#     src/app/build/[slug]/page.tsx
#     src/app/api/build/route.ts
#     src/app/api/build/why-not/route.ts
#     src/app/api/v1/build/route.ts
# and /build and /counter then 404'd in production while every other route
# worked, because the files were never shipped. Keep the leading slashes.
.next/
node_modules/
.vercel/
.env*
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo
/coverage/
/out/
/build/
